+# AN-900: Record a consent for a person (T3-AC-004)
+
+- **Jira:** AN-900
+- **Gate:** design (trigger 2: new event `identity.consent-changed`; trigger 3: new table `identity.consent`, first use of the personal data category `preference`)
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:** pending (a second person, before the merge)
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** identity. Touches: `apps/worker` (wires the consent store); other modules may subscribe to `identity.consent-changed`
+
+## Context
+
+The platform records the consents of a person, for example for marketing e-mails, and head office must prove each consent (T4 privacy controls). `identity` owns consents (architecture section 4, T3-D-009). Decision: [ADR-0017](../../adr/0017-consent-changed-event.md).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+| ID | Test |
+|---|---|
+| T3-AC-004 | `packages/core/src/identity/consent.test.ts`, `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file** (`packages/core/src/identity/AGENTS.md`):
+  - `createIdentity({ repo, consents, bus, clock })`: new required dependency `consents: ConsentRepository`.
+  - `.recordConsent({ personId, purpose, textVersion, channel, granted }): Promise<ConsentRecord>`. Throws `PersonNotFoundError` for an unknown person, `TypeError` for an empty purpose or text version or an unknown channel.
+  - `.currentConsent(personId, purpose): Promise<ConsentRecord | null>`.
+  - `.consentHistory(personId): Promise<ConsentRecord[]>`, oldest first.
+  - New exports: `InMemoryConsentRepository`, `CONSENT_CHANNELS`, `PersonNotFoundError`, types `ConsentRecord`, `ConsentRepository`, `ConsentChanged`, `ConsentChannel`, `RecordConsentInput`.
+  - Invariants: consent records are append-only; the current decision per purpose is the latest record (T3-AC-004).
+- **Contracts:** event `identity.consent-changed`, payload `{ consentId, personId, purpose }`, published after the record is stored. No ERP operation.
+- **Schema:** table `identity.consent`, index on `(person_id, purpose)`:
+
+| Column | Type | Personal | Category | Purpose | Owner | Retention |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `id` | uuid, primary key | no | | | | |
+| `person_id` | uuid, references `identity.person.id` | no (pseudonymous key, like `person.id`) | | | | |
+| `purpose` | text | no (a catalogue value such as `marketing-email`; the choice is `granted`) | | | | |
+| `text_version` | text | no (a version of a legal text) | | | | |
+| `channel` | text: `web`, `advisor`, `import` | yes | preference | Prove the consent decision of the person | identity | account lifetime + 3 years |
+| `granted` | boolean | yes | preference | as above | identity | account lifetime + 3 years |
+| `decided_at` | timestamptz | yes | preference | as above | identity | account lifetime + 3 years |
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- T3-AC-004 "type" maps to `purpose`, "source" to `channel`, "date" to `decidedAt`, "withdrawal" to a record with `granted: false`. Mapping only, not a contradiction.
+- `purpose` is a free, trimmed, non-empty string (for example `marketing-email`): the story names no list of purposes, and the screens that define them are out of scope.
+- `decidedAt` is the time of the call (`clock.now()`). The migration of old consents with their original dates is out of scope; it may need an explicit time later.
+- `channel` is validated at runtime too, because the input comes from screens and imports.
+- The returned and stored records are frozen; the repository port has no update or delete.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- The consent screens, the e-mail marketing tool interface, the migration of old consents.
+- The production Drizzle repository and the database migration (the module has only the in-memory store so far, like `person`).
+
+## Open questions
+
+None.
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
