 |---|---|
 | `identity.person` | `email`, `given_name`, `family_name` |
+| `identity.consent` | `channel`, `granted`, `decided_at` (category `preference`). `purpose` is a catalogue value, not personal |
 
 ## Events <!-- verified: events -->
 
 | Event | Direction | Payload |
 |---|---|---|
 | `identity.person-registered` | Emits | `personId`, `brand` |
+| `identity.consent-changed` | Emits | `consentId`, `personId`, `purpose`. The decision is read with `currentConsent` ([ADR-0017](../../../../docs/adr/0017-consent-changed-event.md)) |
 
 ## Invariants
 
 - One person record per e-mail address. The e-mail is stored in lower case (T3-AC-003).
 - At most one ERP customer number per person (T3-AC-003).
+- Consent records are append-only: never changed or deleted; a new decision adds a record. The current decision per purpose is the latest record (T3-AC-004).
+- A consent record names a registered person, a purpose, a text version and a channel from `CONSENT_CHANNELS` (T3-AC-004).
 - ERP master data comes through the `integration` module, never from the ERP port.
 
